Check whether a proposed new identity actually refers to an identity already stored in the supplied registry.

An identity represents one continuing real-world subject. A name alone is not a unique identity key. Compare every
supplied registry identity using explicit aliases or renames, or a stable name together with defining history.

Return `existing` when exactly one stored identity matches. Return `review_required` with every plausible registry ID
when the evidence cannot distinguish among matches or between an existing and distinct identity. Return `distinct`
when no stored identity is plausible. Explain the decision from the supplied source evidence and registry facts, and
return schema-valid JSON.
